      "text": "$1: \\sqrt{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "j0JQL",
      "text": "1: 2",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "VBV9r",
      "text": "$1: \\sqrt{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The horizontal component of earth's magnetic field is given by, $H=R \\cos \\delta$\r\nwhere, $\\delta$ is the angle of dip so $H_{1}=R \\cos 30^{\\circ}$ and $\\mathrm{H}_{2}=\\mathrm{Rcos} 45^{\\circ}$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\frac{H_{1}}{H_{2}}=\\frac{R \\cos 30^{\\circ}}{R \\cos 45^{\\circ}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3} / 2}{1 / \\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
    "image": null
  },
